 	-Discuss the considerations that went into the choice of your RF design (floor planning,
	slice width, hierarchy partition, etc).

Based on the provided schematics, we performed extensive transistor sizing on the heavily loaded nodes along the critical speed path. In particular, we optimised the output inverters of the driver cell, the output inverter of the master latch, the output transmission gate of the slave latch, and the inverter driving WEM. The NMOS width was fixed at 0.36 µm, while the corresponding PMOS devices were scaled by factors of 3.53 (kWECLK), 3.45 (kWECLKb), 3.73, and 1, respectively, to balance rise and fall delays under load.

These sizing factors were iteratively refined based on transient simulation results. The values reported above reflect the final optimised dimensions.

For the layout, alternating VDD and VSS rails were implemented to achieve a compact and routing-efficient floor-plan. Additionally, bulk ties were inserted at 20 µm intervals to ensure proper substrate biasing and improve latch-up robustness.